    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 130,
      "topLeftY": 259,
      "bottomRightX": 605,
      "bottomRightY": 290,
      "content": "In the following, as the simplest example, the anharmonic oscillator will be treated:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 312,
      "topLeftY": 293,
      "bottomRightX": 604,
      "bottomRightY": 312,
      "content": "$$\\ddot {x} + \\omega_ {0} ^ {2} x + \\lambda x ^ {2} = 0 \\tag {39}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 130,
      "topLeftY": 317,
      "bottomRightX": 605,
      "bottomRightY": 350,
      "content": "Classically, this equation can be satisfied by a Anzatz for the solution of the form:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 141,
      "topLeftY": 362,
      "bottomRightX": 604,
      "bottomRightY": 379,
      "content": "$$x = \\lambda a _ {0} + a _ {1} \\cos \\omega t + \\lambda a _ {2} \\cos 2 \\omega t + \\lambda^ {2} a _ {3} \\cos 3 \\omega t + \\dots + \\lambda^ {\\tau - 1} a _ {\\tau} \\cos \\tau \\omega t \\tag {40}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 130,
      "topLeftY": 388,
      "bottomRightX": 605,
      "bottomRightY": 439,
      "content": "where the $a$ are power series in $\\lambda$, the first terms of which are independent from $\\lambda$. Quantum theoretically, we try an analogous Ansatz representing $x$ with terms of the form",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 166,
      "topLeftY": 447,
      "bottomRightX": 604,
      "bottomRightY": 481,
      "content": "$$\\begin{array}{l} \\lambda a (n, n) \\quad ; \\quad a (n, n - 1) \\cos \\omega (n, n - 1) t \\quad ; \\quad \\lambda a (n, n - 2) t \\quad ; \\\\ \\dots \\quad \\lambda^ {\\tau - 1} a (n, n - \\tau) \\cos \\omega (n, n - \\tau) t \\quad \\dots \\end{array} \\tag {41}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 130,
      "topLeftY": 490,
      "bottomRightX": 604,
      "bottomRightY": 525,
      "content": "The recursion formulae for the determination of $a$ and $\\omega$ (up to order $\\lambda$) according to Eq. 16,17 or Eq. 20, 21 are:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 334,
      "topLeftY": 550,
      "bottomRightX": 406,
      "bottomRightY": 568,
      "content": "Classically:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 272,
      "topLeftY": 574,
      "bottomRightX": 604,
      "bottomRightY": 671,
      "content": "$$\\left. \\begin{array}{c} \\omega_ {0} ^ {2} a _ {0} (n) + \\frac {a _ {1} ^ {2} (n)}{2} = 0; \\\\ - \\omega^ {2} + \\omega_ {0} ^ {2} = 0; \\\\ (- 4 \\omega^ {2} + \\omega_ {0} ^ {2}) a _ {2} (n) + \\frac {a _ {1} ^ {2}}{2} = 0; \\\\ (- 9 \\omega^ {2} + \\omega_ {0} ^ {2}) a _ {3} (n) + a _ {1} a _ {2} = 0; \\\\ . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\end{array} \\right\\} \\tag {42}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 297,
      "topLeftY": 677,
      "bottomRightX": 440,
      "bottomRightY": 693,
      "content": "Quantum theoretically:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 141,
      "topLeftY": 699,
      "bottomRightX": 615,
      "bottomRightY": 812,
      "content": "$$\\left. \\begin{array}{c} \\omega_ {0} ^ {2} a _ {0} (n) + \\frac {a ^ {2} (n + 1 , n) + a ^ {2} (n , n - 1)}{4} = 0; \\\\ - \\omega^ {2} (n, n - 1) + \\omega_ {0} ^ {2} = 0; \\\\ \\left[ - \\omega^ {2} (n, n - 2) + \\omega_ {0} ^ {2} \\right] a (n, n - 2) + \\frac {a (n , n - 1) a (n - 1 , n - 2)}{2} = 0; \\\\ \\left[ - \\omega^ {2} (n, n - 3) + \\omega_ {0} ^ {2} \\right] a (n, n - 3) + \\frac {a (n , n - 2) a (n - 1 , n - 3)}{2} + \\frac {a (n , n - 2) a (n - 2 , n - 3)}{2} = 0; \\\\ . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\quad . \\end{array} \\right\\} \\tag {43}$$",
